// D2255 (plumb PL-025) — a non-empty `u8[]` list literal, delivered everywhere. Nothing in
// `[1, 200]` says `u8`: only the destination does, so every position has to thread the packed
// byte-list kind to the literal. The map value slot did not (`m[k] = [1, 200]` built the i32
// list into a `(ref null $u8list)` vals cell), which is the row this template was written for.
//
// The PROOF reads the second element, so a cell that built the wrong backing cannot print 200.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/matrix.py, whose docstring is the spec.
// @@VALUE@@
[1, 200]
// @@TYPE@@
u8[]
// @@TEST@@
v.length == 2
// @@HIT@@
print(v[1])
// @@MISS@@
print(0)
// @@WANT@@
200
// @@SKIP@@
return_inferred: an un-annotated function returns the literal at its own type, `i32[]`, which is not a `u8[]`
